  "notes": "Per-call cost factors into (1) shift normalisation and dedup over |shifts| with O(|shifts|^2) due to the linear `seen.contains` lookup — kept linear because |shifts| is typically <= 10 and the bool[n] table version would allocate n bools per call, (2) edge enumeration which is exactly the sum of `limit` values across canonical shifts (n for most, n/2 for an even-n undirected antipodal shift), and (3) Graph::new + add_edges canonicalisation. Throughput tops out in the 20-27 Medge/s band for n >= 1000 where Graph::add_edges dominates. Small-n shapes sit at 0.6-2.2 us, mostly in Graph::new and add_edges. No allocator hot path beyond the edge Vec growth which is preallocated to `n * |canonical shifts|`."
